  "extraction_notes": "The catalyst system 'BMTM 4a' is described as a mixture or complex containing the red-drawn squaramide 4a, KHMDS, and 1,5-diaminopentane. Compound 10p is an N-acetylated dipeptide fragment (Ac-Val-Val-OH), and 7a is an amide of the nucleobase-containing amino acid L-willardiine (or its isomer). The reaction entry 4a yields a single stereoisomer of the tripeptide analogue 11, while the EDCI control gives a 50:50 mixture of diastereomers. Stereochemistry for 10p, 7a, and 11 was assumed to be all-(S) based on typical L-amino acid conventions and the note about stereochemical purity. For 4b and 4c, no conversion was observed."
